reported to the NPI (above the reporting thresholds for its substances), in all states and territories, including facilities that have since stopped reporting (see latest_report_year)', 'terms': "The business name, ABN, street address and website are left out because some facilities are family businesses or farms. A facility's emissions per substance are in the NPI's own reports (latest_report_url).", 'data_date': '2026-11-25', 'data_date_source': "the day the atlas downloaded the publisher's file"}}, {'protocol': 'landing', 'url': 'https://data.gov.au/data/dataset/npi'}], '_ctx': {'publisher': 'Department of Climate Change, Energy, the Environment and Water (National Pollutant Inventory)', 'publisher_type': 'central-gov', 'country': 'AU', 'seed_catalog': 'curated:files.yaml', 'discovered_via': 'curated'}}, {'kind': 'record', 'id': 'ea-epr-industrial-sites', 'title': 'Environmental permits for industrial installations, England (Environment Agency)', 'publisher': 'Environment Agency', 'publisher_type': 'public-body', 'country': 'GB', 'abstract': 'Installations in England permitted by the Environment Agency under the Environmental Permitting Regulations (the industrial emissions regime): power stations, refineries, chemical works, cement, metals, food and drink, landfills and large waste treatment, and intensive pig and poultry farms. One point per permit. Status is Effective for permits in force, or Surrendered, Revoked, Expired (Inactive), Closure & Aftercare and similar for ended ones; primary_activity is the main activity (e.g. "Intensive Farming; > 40,000 Poultry", "Recovery Of Waste; Hazardous Waste >10T") and activities lists all of them. Operator names and addresses are not in this copy. 6,333 features; left out: 8 records without a location; 1,861 records excluded (administrative duplicates (superseded, consolidated or regulatory-change versions of a permit) and refused applications). Hosted by the atlas as a copy of the publisher\'s download; cite as: Environmental Permitting Regulations - Industrial Sites, Environment Agency.', 'licence': 'Environment Agency Conditional Licence (https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/environment-agency-conditional-licence/environment-agency-conditional-licence): copy, publish, distribute, adapt and use commercially, with attribution. Special conditions on this dataset: the licence lasts one year and ends without notice, and the data includes personal data (individuals and sites operated by individuals), for which whoever passes it on is responsible under data protection law.', 'landing_page': 'https://www.data.gov.uk/dataset/b5b5a07f-c646-4d99-a210-e337fcc60470/environmental-permitting-regulations-industrial-sites', 'bbox': [-6.45, 49.8666, 1.7614, 55.7621], 'geometry_type': 'point', 'concepts_hint': ['pollution-source'], 'endpoints': [{'protocol': 'geojson', 'url': 'https://pushpingeo.github.io/ai-living-world-atlas/data/f/ea-epr-industrial-sites/index.json', 'format': 'GeoJSON tiles', 'info': {'name_field': 'Installation_Name', 'code_field': 'Permit_Number', 'status_field': 'Status', 'class_field': 'primary_activity', 'date_field': 'Permit_Effective_From_Date', 'nation': 'England', 'completeness': 'complete', 'completeness_note': "all of England; every installation permit in the EA's register, in force or ended (surrendered, revoked, expired), not only current ones", 'terms': "Operator names and street addresses are left out of this copy because some operators are private individuals; look a permit up on the EA's public register by its number if the operator is needed. Re-read the licence by Nov 2027.", 'data_date': '2026-11-24', 'data_date_source': "the day the atlas downloaded the publisher's file"}}, {'protocol': 'landing', 'url': 'https://www.data.gov.uk/dataset/b5b5a07f-c646-4d99-a210-e337fcc60470/environmental-permitting-regulations-industrial-sites'}], '_ctx': {'publisher': 'Environment Agency', 'publisher_type': 'public-body', 'country': 'GB', 'seed_catalog': 'curated:files.yaml', 'discovered_via': 'curated'}}, {'kind': 'record', 'id': 'ea-epr-waste-sites', 'title': 'Environmental permits for waste sites, England (Environment Agency)', 'publisher': 'Environment Agency', 'publisher_type': 'public-body', 'country': 'GB', 'abstract': 'Waste operations in England permitted by the Environment Agency (Environmental Permitting Regulations, and waste management licences before them): landfills, transfer stations, treatment, recycling, metal recycling, composting and others. One point per permit. STAT_SDESC is Issued for permits in force, or Surrendered, Expired, Revoked, Closure and similar for ended ones (an ended landfill permit can still mark a past landfill); licence_type is the EA\'s type (e.g. "Non Hazardous LF", "Household, Commercial & Industrial Waste T Stn"); LIC_EFFD, LIC_SURD, LIC_RVKD and LIC_EXPD are the effective, surrender, revocation and expiry dates. Holder names and addresses are not in this copy. 19,092 features; left out: 3 records without a location; 616 records excluded (superseded versions of a permit). Hosted by the atlas as a copy of the publisher\'s download; cite as: Environmental Permitting Regulations - Waste Sites, Environment Agency.', 'licence': 'Environment Agency Conditional Licence (https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/environment-agency-conditional-licence/environment-agency-conditional-licence): copy, publish, distribute, adapt and use commercially, with attribution. Special conditions on this dataset: the licence lasts one year and ends without notice, and the data includes personal data (individuals and sites operated by individuals), for which whoever passes it on is responsible under data protection law.', 'landing_page': 'https://www.data.gov.uk/dataset/e2cc8101-d8b7-434d-a26a-9115061bb57c/environmental-permitting-regulations-waste-sites', 'bbox': [-6.45, 49.8666, 1.7609, 55.8054], 'geometry_type': 'point', 'concepts_hint': ['pollution-source', 'waste'], 'endpoints': [{'protocol': 'geojson', 'url': 'https://pushpingeo.github.io/ai-living-world-atlas/data/f/ea-epr-waste-sites/index.json', 'format': 'GeoJSON tiles', 'info': {'name_field': 'LIC_SITE', 'code_field': 'LIC_NMBR', 'status_field': 'STAT_SDESC', 'class_field': 'licence_type', 'date_field': 'LIC_EFFD', 'class_values': ['Issued', 'Surrendered', 'Expired', 'Revoked', 'Closure', 'Part Suspended', 'Part revoke', 'Suspended', 'Surr Part'], 'nation': 'England', 'completeness': 'complete', 'completeness_note': "all of England; every waste permit and old waste management licence in the EA's register, current or ended", 'terms': "Licence holder names, contact details and street addresses are left out of this copy because some holders are private individuals; look a permit up on the EA's public register by its number if the holder is needed. Re-read the licence by Nov 2027.", 'data_date': '2026-11-24', 'data_date_source': "the day the atlas downloaded the publisher's file"}}, {'protocol': 'landing', 'url': 'https://www.data.gov.uk/dataset/e2cc8101-d8b7-434d-a26a-9115061bb57c/environmental-permitting-regulations-waste-sites'}], '_ctx': {'publisher': 'Environment Agency', 'publisher_type': 'public-body', 'country': 'GB', 'seed_catalog': 'curated:files.yaml', 'discovered_via': 'curated'}}, {'kind': 'record', 'id': 'ea-pollution-incidents', 'title': 'Serious environmental pollution incidents (Category 1 and 2), England, 2001 to date (Environment Agency)', 'publisher': 'Environment Agency', 'publisher_type': 'public-body', 'country': 'GB', 'abstract': 'Substantiated environmental pollution incidents in England that the Environment Agency rated Category 1 (major) or Category 2 (significant) for their impact on water, land or air, from 2001 to the latest quarter. One point per incident at its confirmed location. EIL_WATER, EIL_LAND and EIL_AIR give the impact category on each (an incident is in the set if any of them is 1 or 2); pollutant_types and pollutants list what was released (e.g. "Sewage Materials", "Crude Sewage", "Chemical Odour"); NOT_DATE is when it was reported. An incident near a site does not mean the site\'s owner was responsible. 17,507 features. Hosted by the atlas as a copy of the publisher\'s download; cite as: Environmental Pollution Incidents (Category 1 and 2), Environment Agency.', 'licence': 'Environment Agency Conditional Licence (https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/environment-agency-conditional-licence/environment-agency-conditional-licence): copy, publish, distribute, adapt and use commercially, with attribution. Special conditions on this dataset: the licence lasts one year and ends without notice, and the data includes personal data (individuals and sites operated by individuals), for which whoever passes it on is responsible under data protection law.', 'landing_page': 'https://www.data.gov.uk/dataset/c8625e18-c329-4032-b4c7-444b33af6780/environmental-pollution-incidents-category-1-and-2', 'bbox': [-6.2923, 49.915, 2.0291, 55.7654], 'geometry_type': 'point', 'concepts_hint': ['pollution-source', 'water-quality'], 'endpoints': [{'protocol': 'geojson', 'url': 'https://pushpingeo.github.io/ai-living-world-atlas/data/f/ea-pollution-incidents/index.json', 'format': 'GeoJSON tiles', 'info': {'code_field': 'NOT_ID', 'date_field': 'NOT_DATE', 'class_field': 'EIL_WATER', 'class_values': ['Category 1 (Major)', 'Category 2 (Significant)', 'Category 3 (Minor)', 'Category 4 (No Impact)'], 'nation': 'England', 'completeness': 'complete', 'completeness_note': "all of England from 2001; only substantiated incidents with a Category 1 or 2 impact on water, land or air. Minor incidents aren't in it", 'terms': "An incident at or near a site does not mean the site's owner or operator caused it. Re-read the licence by Nov 2027.", 'data_date': '2026-11-24', 'data_date_source': "the day the atlas downloaded the publisher's file"}}, {'protocol': 'landing', 'url': 'https://www.data.gov.uk/dataset/c8625e18-c329-4032-b4c7-444b33af6780/environmental-pollution-inc